{
  "name": "Mutation",
  "icon": "hexalia:mutavis",
  "category": "hexalia:core_mechanics",
  "sortnum": 4,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Mutation",
      "text": "Mutation is the process of transforming natural blocks into new forms using Mutavis. Through it, hidden aspects of the world are revealed, allowing common materials to take on magical properties."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Using Mutavis",
      "anchor": "usage",
      "text": "Mutavis can be applied directly to blocks to trigger a transformation. The result depends on the material, often revealing new plants, altered terrain, or unexpected resources."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Area Mutation",
      "anchor": "area",
      "text": "When used on a $(l:hexalia:content/enchanted_plants#morphora)Morphora$(/l), Mutavis spreads outward, affecting nearby blocks at once. This allows large-scale transformation of the surrounding environment."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "On Results",
      "anchor": "results",
      "text": "Mutations may either replace the original block or produce their result as an item. This behavior can be configured, allowing different approaches to resource gathering."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Automation",
      "anchor": "automation",
      "text": "Mutavis can be applied using dispensers, enabling automated mutation of blocks or Morphora flowers when supplied with the necessary resources."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "On Discovery",
      "text": "Different materials respond differently to Mutavis. Plants, stone, and earth each reveal their own transformations, encouraging experimentation across the natural world."
    },
